THOUGHT: NullAway complains because get() passes a literal null to get(Actor), which it currently believes requires a non-null parameter. The method is documented and annotated with @Null to allow null, but NullAway likely doesn’t recognize com.badlogic.gdx.utils.Null as a nullable annotation. To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I’ll add a no-arg abstract get() method and have the existing get(@Null Actor) default implementation delegate to it when context is null. This avoids passing null while preserving API semantics. Then I’ll run the compile task to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '30,41c\public abstract class Value {
  /** Calls {@link #get(Actor)} with null. */
  public float get() {
    return get((Actor) null);
  }

  /**
   * @param context May be null.
   */
  public float get(@Null Actor context) {
    return getImpl(context);
  }

  /** Implementation method that may assume non-null context if desired. */
  protected abstract float getImpl(@Null Actor context);
}' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Value.java && sed -i '49,60c\t  public static class Fixed extends Value {
	    static final Fixed[] cache = new Fixed[111];

	    private final float value;

	    public Fixed(float value) {
	      this.value = value;
	    }

	    @Override
	    protected float getImpl(@Null Actor context) {
	      return value;
	    }

	    public String toString() {
	      return Float.toString(value);
	    }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Value.java && sed -i '78,160s/public float get(@Null Actor [a-zA-Z]*)/public float getImpl(@Null Actor \1)/g' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Value.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway: .*errors" new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

